                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ive been trying this game for some time and always quiting levels and starting over again.\nI have to be honest, I dont really like it.\nNot that its a bad game overall - It has great music, a cool story, and super cool \"feeling\" to it.\n\nBut the gameplay... it feels rather unfair...\n\nI think its not the difficulty itself that makes it unfair, but the way traps and bullets work.\nThey shoot over and over again in patterns, and they dont stop when you die. The level loops endlessly and dying does not reset it.\n\nFor me those \"patterns\" are just way too hard to decrypt, most of the times I just sit there for 2minutes trying to figure out how to clear the level so that you perfectly mix with the pattern.\nBut thats just not possible. there are so many bullets splitting there and flying there its just too much going on. When I try to make a plan on how to jump it never works no matter how hard I think of it. The music does not help either, it rather fucks up my jumping timing.\n\nSo 90% of the levels I just rush in over and over again untill im lucky to slide throught the objects and finish the level.\nI dont feel satisfied at all. There is no \"i just solved that lvl\" feeling. \n\nI really can not not recommand it, because it has so much power in story and creativity. ....\nBut i cant, it feels unplayable to me, and does not do what it is supposed to do.",
